00:00:02.830 --> 00:00:05.942
Today's message is Choose Anything.

00:00:05.942 --> 00:00:07.555
Over to you, Neil Strauss.

00:00:07.555 --> 00:00:09.888
(swooshing)

00:00:10.888 --> 00:00:13.186
(rooster crowing)

00:00:13.186 --> 00:00:15.857
♫ I wake up every mornin'

00:00:15.857 --> 00:00:19.274
♫ Expresso keep me goin'

00:00:20.136 --> 00:00:22.209
- Choose anything.

00:00:22.209 --> 00:00:24.020
It doesn't even matter,
just choose anything.

00:00:24.020 --> 00:00:27.143
So, here's an example, so
I wish I could almost draw.

00:00:27.143 --> 00:00:29.026
But, I'll tell you what.

00:00:29.026 --> 00:00:30.017
Let's see, what can I use as a,--

00:00:30.017 --> 00:00:30.892
- [Chase] Sir.

00:00:30.892 --> 00:00:32.175
- We'll use the back of this couch here.

00:00:32.175 --> 00:00:33.008
This is you.

00:00:33.008 --> 00:00:34.684
Are we filming that?
- [Chase] Sure.

00:00:34.684 --> 00:00:35.836
- I don't even know if it's
going to be worthwhile.

00:00:35.836 --> 00:00:36.669
But we'll say it is.
- [Chase] Try it.

00:00:36.669 --> 00:00:37.554
- This is you, right,

00:00:37.554 --> 00:00:39.061
and you're like "I don't know what to do."

00:00:39.061 --> 00:00:39.894
"I'm not sure what to do."

00:00:39.894 --> 00:00:41.905
And you're just sitting
here, doing nothing.

00:00:41.905 --> 00:00:43.055
Right, this little white stain,

00:00:43.055 --> 00:00:44.379
I don't even know what it is.
- (Chase laughs)

00:00:44.379 --> 00:00:46.451
- It's Lemar Burtons' back sweat.(laughs)

00:00:46.451 --> 00:00:47.284
Is that his name?

00:00:47.284 --> 00:00:48.117
- [Chase] Levar.

00:00:48.117 --> 00:00:49.579
- Levar Furton, I don't know who,

00:00:49.579 --> 00:00:50.984
it could be anyone's sweat right there.

00:00:50.984 --> 00:00:52.714
So that's a little piece of sweat,

00:00:52.714 --> 00:00:54.235
toiling and trying to decide what to do.

00:00:54.235 --> 00:00:57.033
But then just choose frigging anything.

00:00:57.033 --> 00:00:58.728
Let's just say, "Oh, I
want to be an actor."

00:00:58.728 --> 00:00:59.796
Just, who cares?

00:00:59.796 --> 00:01:00.737
Maybe you don't, I don't know.

00:01:00.737 --> 00:01:01.596
Just choose the one thing.

00:01:01.596 --> 00:01:03.442
So you choose one thing and
now you have a goal, right.

00:01:03.442 --> 00:01:04.429
Just choose a goal, it doesn't matter,

00:01:04.429 --> 00:01:06.309
and now maybe you're going
to start going to auditions,

00:01:06.309 --> 00:01:07.714
your going to auditions.

00:01:07.714 --> 00:01:10.059
And then wait, you got a
job but it's voiceover work.

00:01:10.059 --> 00:01:11.453
Or maybe it's on radio.

00:01:11.453 --> 00:01:12.486
You got a little radio gig, right.

00:01:12.486 --> 00:01:14.146
So now you're like "Oh radio's fun,

00:01:14.146 --> 00:01:15.029
"I'm going to be a radio host."

00:01:15.029 --> 00:01:16.317
And that's your next goal.

00:01:16.317 --> 00:01:19.336
And then you get a call to
do a voiceover on a cartoon,

00:01:19.336 --> 00:01:21.368
or something and you're like
"OK, I'll be a cartoon voice."

00:01:21.368 --> 00:01:23.214
And guess what, now
you're actually moving,

00:01:23.214 --> 00:01:25.800
and maybe you will end up being a,

00:01:25.800 --> 00:01:27.759
the voice of whatever,

00:01:27.759 --> 00:01:29.678
on the next Pixar movie,
or something like that.

00:01:29.678 --> 00:01:30.808
- [Chase] Eugene Mirman is a friend,

00:01:30.808 --> 00:01:33.118
he's the voice in Bob's Burgers.

00:01:33.118 --> 00:01:35.127
- Yeah, yeah, exactly,
along with (finger snaps),

00:01:35.127 --> 00:01:37.437
yeah there's so many good
John H, John Benjamin,

00:01:37.437 --> 00:01:38.270
is that his name?

00:01:38.270 --> 00:01:39.103
- [Chase] Oowoo.

00:01:39.103 --> 00:01:40.512
- He was also in Home
Movies, he's great, anyway.

00:01:40.512 --> 00:01:44.772
But the point is, just choose
one thing to move toward,

00:01:44.772 --> 00:01:48.186
and then just go with the path
and you'll end up somewhere,

00:01:48.186 --> 00:01:50.368
but if you stay in here
trying to decide what to do,

00:01:50.368 --> 00:01:51.646
you'll still be here in a year,

00:01:51.646 --> 00:01:52.760
two years, three years, four years.

00:01:52.760 --> 00:01:55.686
Just choose something you
kind of like and don't hate.

00:01:55.686 --> 00:01:56.951
And then start moving toward it,

00:01:56.951 --> 00:01:58.728
and you'll find that the
course and path of life

00:01:58.728 --> 00:02:00.481
will bring you exactly
where you're supposed to be.

00:02:00.481 --> 00:02:03.488
Did that work on the compact of the couch?

00:02:03.488 --> 00:02:04.672
- I think this is so important

00:02:04.672 --> 00:02:07.714
because too many entrepreneurs
spend so much time

00:02:07.714 --> 00:02:09.912
planning and planning and
planning and planning.

00:02:09.912 --> 00:02:13.681
They won't do anything until
they have the perfect plan.

00:02:13.681 --> 00:02:17.873
And you need to understand
that there is no such thing,

00:02:17.873 --> 00:02:19.672
as a perfect plan.

00:02:19.672 --> 00:02:21.518
You need to start doing.

00:02:21.518 --> 00:02:23.283
You need to start taking action.

00:02:23.283 --> 00:02:25.988
I look at my business today
and it's nowhere close

00:02:25.988 --> 00:02:27.764
to what I thought I was going to do.

00:02:27.764 --> 00:02:30.063
I never planned on
having a popular website.

00:02:30.063 --> 00:02:32.037
I never wanted to be a YouTuber.

00:02:32.037 --> 00:02:34.707
I didn't even want to
write a book, at the start.

00:02:34.707 --> 00:02:36.425
I never planned on any of
these things happening.

00:02:36.425 --> 00:02:38.492
It wasn't part of my dream plan.

00:02:38.492 --> 00:02:40.257
I thought I was going to be a speaker.

00:02:40.257 --> 00:02:41.731
And I showed up when I did my first event

00:02:41.731 --> 00:02:45.272
and three people showed up,
and I just loved it so much.

00:02:45.272 --> 00:02:47.687
On paper it looked like a terrible idea.

00:02:47.687 --> 00:02:48.999
You can't get more than three people

00:02:48.999 --> 00:02:50.508
to show up to a free event,

00:02:50.508 --> 00:02:51.623
how are you ever going to turn this

00:02:51.623 --> 00:02:53.585
into a money making business?

00:02:53.585 --> 00:02:56.093
Quit now, save yourself
a lot of frustration

00:02:56.093 --> 00:02:58.548
and headache, and go do something else.

00:02:58.548 --> 00:03:01.062
I think it's so important that you start.

00:03:01.062 --> 00:03:03.209
I never thought I was going to run,

00:03:03.209 --> 00:03:05.845
and own a Salsa Dance School.

00:03:05.845 --> 00:03:08.600
I didn't do any dancing growing up.

00:03:08.600 --> 00:03:10.978
And I came out of a relationship,

00:03:10.978 --> 00:03:12.905
and I wanted to pick up dancing,

00:03:12.905 --> 00:03:15.134
and I walked in to a Salsa class,

00:03:15.134 --> 00:03:17.770
and I'm too tall and
I don't speak Spanish,

00:03:17.770 --> 00:03:19.453
and I've never heard the music before,

00:03:19.453 --> 00:03:22.396
and I take huge steps, and
I'm learning as an adult.

00:03:22.396 --> 00:03:25.101
All these things against
me in the perfect plan,

00:03:25.101 --> 00:03:27.887
and here I am, fast forward,
how many years later,

00:03:27.887 --> 00:03:28.720
I now run,

00:03:29.582 --> 00:03:32.868
maybe the largest Salsa Dance
School in North America.

00:03:32.868 --> 00:03:35.213
The key is that you start.

00:03:35.213 --> 00:03:36.978
And that you adjust.

00:03:36.978 --> 00:03:38.638
You can have a plan.

00:03:38.638 --> 00:03:41.552
It's not just, have zero plan.

00:03:41.552 --> 00:03:44.025
You can have a plan that
you think makes sense,

00:03:44.025 --> 00:03:45.291
and that works.

00:03:45.291 --> 00:03:47.009
And then go do something about it.

00:03:47.009 --> 00:03:48.820
Stop just thinkin' about it.

00:03:48.820 --> 00:03:51.664
Stop just sittin' at
home planning more plans.

00:03:51.664 --> 00:03:54.056
Plans on top of plans on top of plans.

00:03:54.056 --> 00:03:56.146
Go do something about it.

00:03:56.146 --> 00:03:58.375
'Cuz some of your assumptions
are going to be wrong.

00:03:58.375 --> 00:04:00.196
Because once you get out into the market,

00:04:00.196 --> 00:04:01.306
you're going to discover new things,

00:04:01.306 --> 00:04:03.495
that you couldn't of
planned for or prepared for.

00:04:03.495 --> 00:04:05.887
Because opportunities
are going to come to you.

00:04:05.887 --> 00:04:07.651
And maybe that's the right one to jump on

00:04:07.651 --> 00:04:09.079
to help drive you forward.

00:04:09.079 --> 00:04:09.912
Start!

00:04:10.798 --> 00:04:12.237
And adjust.

00:04:12.237 --> 00:04:13.352
So the question of the day today is,

00:04:13.352 --> 00:04:14.352
I'm curious,

00:04:15.260 --> 00:04:18.518
"What was something that
you didn't see coming?

00:04:18.518 --> 00:04:20.430
"What's an opportunity you jumped on,

00:04:20.430 --> 00:04:22.319
"that wasn't part of your plan,

00:04:22.319 --> 00:04:24.084
"and that you're doin' right now?"

00:04:24.084 --> 00:04:25.361
I'm super curious to find out.

00:04:25.361 --> 00:04:26.603
Leave in the comments below,

00:04:26.603 --> 00:04:28.077
I'm going to join in the discussion.

